\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{A recovery site}
\date{2026-11-12}

\p{Let #{x} be a vertex of a symmetric digraph carrying the
derived form of \ref{fdip-00PB}. Call #{x} a \newvocab{recovery
site} of rank #{n} when some set #{U} of vertices contains
#{x} and satisfies three conditions. The odd identification of
\ref{fdip-00PO} is available at every vertex of #{U} on the
same #{n} axes, the two weights of each axis are equal units,
and the dot form #{\bar q} is nondegenerate of rank #{n} at
every vertex of #{U}. Both directions of each of those axes
are present on #{U}, so the forward and backward edges may be
identified, and the weights on the two directions agree. The
functions that are affine on #{U} in the sense of
\ref{fdip-00PK} produce odd vectors spanning the free module
of rank #{n}, and the commutator square on the cochains of
the cells whose vertices and one-step shifts lie in #{U}
equals #{-\bar q}.}
